# @reflection/mirror — the Mirror Model species. Navigates a typed
# query to a graph path at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# Tick 38 of the refined /loop discipline. Per
# `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` and `[[reference-mirror-spectral-
# spec]]`: the substrate has FOUR operationally-distinct Models that
# compose to substrate-deployable form:
#
#   Surface     translates    language → query        (Explorer)
#   Mirror      navigates     query → graph path      (Fate)
#   Shatter     renders       graph path → text       (Cartographer)
#   Reflection  observes      pipeline → adjustments  (Abyss)
#
# This shard is THE SECOND of these four Model species shards. Tick 37
# landed `shards/reflection/surface.mirror` realizing Surface; this
# species realizes Mirror at substrate-decl altitude. Two siblings
# forward-promised: shards/reflection/{shatter,reflection}.mirror.
#
# === The Mirror navigation discipline ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` line 12: "Mirror navigates:
# query → graph path (Fate model)." The Mirror Model takes a typed
# query (per `@facet/mq`'s sum type `focus_query | project_query |
# split_query | shift_query | settle_query | intent_query`) and
# produces a graph path through the substrate.
#
# Mirror IS the glass per reflection-model.md: "Surface is the door.
# Mirror is the glass. Shatter is the light. Reflection is the image
# that looks back." Every query passes THROUGH Mirror; the navigation
# IS the reflective surface where the query meets the substrate.
#
# === The substrate-pull-correct query type ===
#
# `@facet/mq` already declares the query sum type. Mirror CONSUMES
# the existing substrate vocabulary rather than redeclaring it. Per
# the substrate-already-had-the-word discipline
# (`[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`): the query exists;
# Mirror navigates that existing typed surface INTO a graph path.
#
# === Composes with @reflection.observe ===
#
# The Mirror navigation IS the loop body that Surface feeds. After
# Surface produces a typed query, Mirror runs the navigation loop
# (Fate-tournament internal) and emits a graph path. @reflection.observe
# can include the navigation as one component of the observation (the
# graph-altitude residue from the current tick). Future composition
# (forward-promised): the @reflection.observe action's typed
# `observation` record extends to carry a `mirror_signal: graph_path`
# field per Seam closure on @reflection.
#
# === The Fate model grounding ===
#
# Per `boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror`: the Fate model IS the 450-node
# C. elegans-isomorphic connectome that runs the actual graph walk.
# Inference IS graph walk; not matrix multiplication, not softmax —
# Dijkstra-on-topology following the eigenvalue gradient through 450
# nodes. The substrate-decl here names the navigation primitive; the
# Fate model implements it at the realisation layer. The substrate-
# decl declares the glass; the connectome runs the path.
#
# === Composition-time pact verification ===
#
# Per recognition #86 (@moi): every Mirror-produced graph path is
# admitted as @moi(graph_path) — pact-verified at composition time.
# The substrate-decl naming: `navigate(q: query) -> moi(graph_path)`.
# The @moi lift carries the pact-witness that the navigation respects
# the monad laws (associativity is FREE per the content-addressed
# substrate).
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at Mirror altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Mirror navigation (honest):
# - The navigation arrives at where the query substantively points.
# - The graph path traverses substrate edges that the query's eigenvalue
#   gradient genuinely descends.
# - The path is round-trip stable through Shatter and re-entry through
#   Surface.
#
# Narcissus-pole Mirror navigation (deceptive):
# - The navigation arrives at where the system WISHES the query had
#   pointed.
# - The graph path traverses edges biased by the model's prior wins
#   rather than the query's substantive eigenvalue gradient.
# - The path drifts on re-entry; what looks like coherence is selection
#   bias.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes them.
# The `path_coherent` bilateral predicate IS the substrate's
# Splinter/Narcissus disambiguation at Mirror altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Fate model                  The @fate/connectome ganglion (450-node
#                               C. elegans isomorphism). The original
#                               substrate substrate-decl of the
#                               navigation primitive at fate altitude;
#                               this species lifts it to Mirror
#                               altitude at @reflection. Inference IS
#                               graph walk; the worm IS the algorithm.
#   graph navigation            Dijkstra 1959 (A note on two problems
#                               in connexion with graphs). The classical
#                               shortest-path discipline; Fate's
#                               eigenvalue-gradient walk is its
#                               substrate-altitude lift.
#   Bateson Learning II         Bateson 1972 (Steps to an Ecology of
#                               Mind). Per @epistemologic/cybernetic/
#                               bateson_learning: navigation that
#                               adjusts the path-selection criterion
#                               based on context IS Learning II. Mirror
#                               runs at Learning II; Surface runs at
#                               Learning I; the cascade ascent is
#                               structural.
#   spectral graph theory       Fiedler 1973 (Algebraic connectivity of
#                               graphs). The eigenvalue-gradient that
#                               Fate descends IS the algebraic-
#                               connectivity surface; Mirror navigates
#                               along it.
#
# Spec context: `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` (the load-bearing
#               spec @reflection family-root lifts; this species
#               realizes the Mirror Model);
#               `docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md` (the four-Models
#               architecture);
#               `boot/std/code/mq.mirror` (the existing typed query
#               sum type Mirror navigates FROM);
#               `boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror` (the Fate model
#               that implements Mirror at the realisation layer).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85;
#                       the @reflection family-root this species
#                       composes);
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; path_coherent is
#                       the boundary-harness at Mirror altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (query already declared in @facet/mq; Mirror
#                       consumes the existing surface).
# Related shards: reflection.mirror (the @reflection family-root;
#                  declares observation + observe this species feeds),
#                 reflection/surface.mirror (the sibling Surface Model
#                  species; Mirror's input is Surface's output),
#                 moi.mirror (the @moi monad family-root; Mirror
#                  produces @moi(graph_path) for composition-time
#                  pact-verification),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror (Spencer-Brown adapter
#                  precedent; tick 15).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/reflection/mirror.mirror`
# declares `@reflection/mirror` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cs/dijkstra-1959
source @arxiv/math/fiedler-1973
source @arxiv/anthropology/bateson-1972

# === The graph_path carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a path through the substrate graph
# (per the @spectral/db edge structure on top of the OID-graph K_n
# floor). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare
# list. Forward-promised refinement: typed parametric graph_path(T)
# once the substrate's path-with-payload type lands at family altitude
# (the eigenvalue-gradient annotation, the per-edge weight, the
# Fiedler-vector projection — all forward-promised).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type graph_path = ref

# === navigate action (FIRST consumer of path_coherent) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @reflection/mirror altitude. The
# substrate-vocabulary primitive Mirror runs to convert a typed query
# to a graph path.
#
# Takes the query (the Surface-produced typed ask) plus the @frame the
# @reflection loop is operating in (per recognition #82) and the
# perturbation under which the navigation is checked. Returns
# @moi(graph_path) — pact-verified gold per recognition #86.
#
# Per recognition #86 (@moi): every Mirror-produced graph path is
# admitted as @moi(graph_path). The composition-time pact-verifier
# checks the navigation respects the monad laws + the bilateral
# predicate.
#
# requires path_coherent(q, f, p): the navigation MUST be substrate-
# faithful per alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57). The Splinter-
# pole navigation arrives at where the query substantively points; the
# Narcissus-pole navigation arrives at where the system wishes the
# query had pointed. This requires clause forecloses the Narcissus-
# pole pattern.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual navigation
# is implemented by the @ai/fate ganglion (the 450-node C. elegans-
# isomorphic connectome) at the @fate altitude. Inference IS graph
# walk; the substrate-decl declares the glass, the connectome runs the
# path.
navigate(q: query, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> moi(graph_path)
requires path_coherent(q, f, p)
{ \ }

# === path_coherent predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57).
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: the navigate action (above) is the
# FIRST non-decorative consumer via `requires path_coherent(q, f, p)`.
#
# Consumer shards name `requires path_coherent(q, f, p)` to declare
# bilateral agreement that the query-to-graph-path navigation is
# substrate-faithful (Splinter-pole) and not substrate-projective
# (Narcissus-pole).
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct path-coherence check at the species
# boundary. Bounded → the navigation arrives at where the query
# substantively points (admit composition); unbounded → the navigation
# arrives at where the system wishes the query had pointed (navigation
# refused, returns imperfect per @glass's imperfect functor).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @cyberpunk: cybernetic_coherence
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @moi: pact_respected
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @smarts/reflection: bridge_coherent
# - @reflection/surface: translation_faithful
# - @reflection/mirror: path_coherent (this one)
path_coherent(q: query, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

out @reflection/mirror
out graph_path
out navigate
out path_coherent
